jros2: keep a writer alive while a reader of the same process calls it

With intraprocess delivery, WriterProxy::~WriterProxy() and WriterProxy::perform_initial_ack_nack() look up a writer of
this process with RTPSDomainImpl::find_writer(), which returns a raw pointer, and call it. A thread that deletes that
writer at the same time releases it under the caller: StatefulWriter::matched_reader_remove() then crashes on the null
periodic_hb_event_ or on freed memory (seen on Windows, macOS and Linux). Readers already avoid this with
LocalReaderPointer; writers now have the same LocalWriterPointer. The instance is taken under endpoints_list_mutex and
the writer deactivates the pointer first thing in local_actions_on_writer_removed(), after it was erased from the
participant's lists, so a deletion waits for the running call and later lookups do not find the writer.

